Do you have what it takes to help keep the lights on for our customers? Come grow your career with a team that powers homes, businesses, and everyday life across the province.  
 Applications are accepted until December 10, 2027. 
 The Opportunity  
 As a valued member of our Customer Relations Team, you will be responsible for implementing the guidelines and procedures associated with the Company's Collection Policy. 
 Key Responsibilities: 
 Contacting customers in person or by phone;
 Making appropriate payment arrangements;
 Servicing, changing, and reprogramming meters that provide electrical service;
 Collecting monthly and special meter readings;
 Collecting payments in the field;
 Updating accounts in our Customer Service System;
 Other related duties.
   Your qualifications include: 
 Degree in Business, or a three-year diploma in Business Management (Accounting), supplemented by experience in a computerized credit and/or collection environment;
 You must hold and maintain a valid driver's license;
 Completion of the Certified Credit Professional designation is an asset;
 You are a highly motivated team player with a strong commitment to safety and customer service;
 An excellent work ethic;
 Effective interpersonal and communication skills.
 You have a strong analytical and project management skills and are able to execute technical tasks with particular attention to detail.
 Compensation: 
 As per the IBEW Clerical Collective Agreement 
 How to Apply 
 If this opportunity sounds like a fit, please click Apply below to begin the application process. Tip: Have your most up-to-date resume ready to help make the process easier. 
 We thank all applicants for their interest; however, only those selected for an interview will be contacted.
 DEI Commitment 
 In support of our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitment and to help us to confirm that we are reaching a wide source of qualified job seekers, we invite all applicants to provide self-identification information on a  voluntary  basis during the recruitment phase. More information on this process is provided within our job application tool.   
 If you require accommodation during the interview process, please let us know. Any information shared will be kept confidential. For questions, please contact Careers@newfoundlandpower.com .
 To Learn More 
 To learn more about Newfoundland Power and what we offer, visit https://careers.newfoundlandpower.com and connect with us on social media for our latest news, employee stories, community activities and updates.

